===Etymology===
''Álfheim'' is a compilation of the words [[álfr]] (elf) and [[heim]] (home) and comes from the Old Norse ''[[Álfheimr]]''. 

===Proper noun===
'''Álfheim'''

# The home of the [[álfar]] ([[elves]], divine beings), in Norse mythology; [[Elfhame]], [[Elfland]].
# Possibly [[heaven]].

